                      (er_reset_helper.s):00001         ; PERF-004 low-RAM gateway for the generated perimeter-reset program.
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00002         ; The boot-synthesized payload occupies physical page $20 and returns here before PAR5 is
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00003         ; restored to the game-state page.  This code must remain within $06B2-$07FF.
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00004         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror begins. Canonical definitions:
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00005         ; wiki/internal/implementation/routine-catalog.html
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00006         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Inputs: Source and destination identities, bounded count or stream metadata, and any required mapped page
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00007         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Outputs: Copied, decoded, merged, cached, or addressed data plus caller-visible pointer progress
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00008         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Clobbers: A, B, D, X, Y, U, and condition codes unless a narrower source-local header is present
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00009         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Reads: The declared source stream, table, framebuffer rows, or metadata record
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00010         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Writes: Only the declared bounded destination record, cache, row range, or scratch fields
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00011         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Side effects: May temporarily map a required GIME page while moving or decoding data
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00012         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Invariants: Counts and destination bounds are honored; any temporary GIME mapping is restored before returning unless the routine contract explicitly states otherwise
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00013         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Inputs: Presentation state, interval timer, input edges, current map, and the selected auxiliary profile
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00014         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Outputs: Updated presentation state and the dispatcher retain/release status when applicable
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00015         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Clobbers: A, B, D, X, Y, U, and condition codes unless a narrower source-local header is present
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00016         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Reads: Presentation direct-page state, cold payloads, authored map streams, and input state
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00017         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Writes: Presentation state, mapped BACK pixels, and presentation-owned persistent metadata
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00018         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Side effects: May retain the foreground interval or produce a complete presentation surface
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00019         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Invariants: Gameplay simulation begins only after release; hidden hydration may prepare initial-stage state and hold it unchanged until release; FRONT publication remains IRQ-owned
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00020         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile root Inputs: Entry-specific machine state and the shared direct-page protocol named by the routine purpose
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00021         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile root Outputs: Control transfers or status values defined by the routine purpose
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00022         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile root Clobbers: A, B, D, X, Y, U, and condition codes unless the caller-facing entry contract states otherwise
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00023         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile root Reads: Always-mapped direct-page protocol state plus the module-owned state required by the selected operation
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00024         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile root Writes: Module-owned state and mapped hardware registers required to establish or dispatch the operation
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00025         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile root Side effects: May change mapping, interrupt, rendering, or lifecycle ownership as stated by the routine purpose
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00026         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile root Invariants: The stack remains balanced and every temporary PAR mapping is restored or deliberately handed off before return
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00027         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract PERIMETER_RESET_HELPER profile=root: Map and invoke the synthesized perimeter reset payload, then restore PAR5.
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00028         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract hold_copy_chunk profile=copy: Copy one bounded chunk while constructing or restoring a held presentation surface.
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00029         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract presentation_attract_phase profile=presentation: Advance the helper-owned attract overlay phase.
                      (er_reset_helper.s):00030         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror ends.
